  "179:93": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "A continuous five-second shot.\n\nThe white 3D Todeok mascot stands quietly on the foreground rock at the lower left, with both feet staying planted on the same spots on the rock and its face and body always facing the camera. After a brief pause, Todeok gently and calmly sways its whole body from side to side once, then gives a small, slow, polite bow of the head toward the camera and returns to its upright pose. Halfway through, it blinks its small round black eyes once. The torso never turns away from the camera.\n\nPreserve the complete mascot from head to feet in every frame. Its white body remains solid and fully opaque, with the same rounded proportions, face, short legs and smooth surfaces.\n\nBoth wings retain their original rounded, fingerless shapes and stay at the sides of the body exactly as in the first frame. The balloon-holding wing keeps its original closed grip throughout; the other wing stays beside the body. Exactly four balloons remain in their original compact arrangement, with the same colors, shapes and sizes. All strings keep their original lengths and remain connected to the same grip. The balloons follow the motion with only a slight, gentle sway.\n\nVery slow, subtle zoom-in at eye level: the camera moves in only slightly and gently toward the carved stone Buddha relief in the center, while Todeok stays fully visible on the left with its balloons. Only a few bamboo leaves move softly in a faint breeze. The carved stone relief and surrounding rocks remain completely still with stable lighting.\n\nNo walking, jumping, floating or climbing. No body enlargement, stretching or deformation. No disappearance, fading, transparency or duplication. No balloon release, rising balloons or detached strings.",
      "clip": [
        "179:84",
        0
      ]
    },
    "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "CLIP Text Encode (Positive Prompt)",
      "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
      "ver": "0.3.45"
    }
  },
